      "content": "got it. so basically, if a neighborhood's majority is shifting from white to a more diverse mix, you'd flag that as a signal for lower growth? just trying to understand the logic—is there a specific \"tipping point\" in the demographic data that you'd use to identify where a neighborhood starts becoming a \"low-value\" zone?",
